# The Python analysis pipeline is not part of the site build, so it never deploys.
#
# The leading slash matters and is not cosmetic. A bare "analysis/" matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, which also excluded data/analysis/ and public/content/analysis/ —
# the published figures the site imports and serves. That broke the production build with
# "Module not found: ./analysis/register-comparison.json" while the local build passed,
# because locally the files were simply there. Anchor the pattern to the repo root.
/analysis/
